UID:10000076-1784361600-1784368800@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Meet Your Plant Neighbors
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC for an exploration of Johnston Mill Nature Preserve!\nWhat plants do we live amongst? What are their names? What are their stories? On this hike\, we'll amble along Robin's\, Bluebird\, and Old Field Bluffs trails\, identifying plants along the way. We'll meet native Piedmont trees\, shrubs\, and herbs in the mixed hardwood forest\, at the edge of New Hope Creek\, and along the sunny powerline easement.\n\nThis will be a 2-3 mile hike with a decent amount of topographical change. This is a free event\, but preregistration is required.\n\n \n\n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/meet-your-plant-neighbors
LOCATION:Johnston Mill Nature Preserve\, 2713 Mt. Sinai Rd.\, Chapel Hill\, North Carolina\, 27514\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
